Before you start coding:
1. Do I understand the task?
2. Do I have the knowledge to complete the task?
3. Are there existing libraries I could use?
4. Do I know where to start?

Writing the code:
1. Never delete anything
2. Create the new features and make sure it works
- You can see what is breaking the code
3. delete ONLY WHEN the new code works perfectly
4. If there is an error, it should always return the error and not a success case.

-------------------------------------------------------

SQL Database:
- mostly used for 'write'

Azure Table Storage (NoSQL - follows AP from CAP Theorum):
- mostly used for 'read' - optimised for fast key-based lookups but can also write
- stores non-relational structured data (structured NoSQL data)
- it is schemaless = each entity has different properties
- In the context of shopping list:
  - PartitionKey = User
  - RowKey = List Items
  - Secondary = Address, Name, List name, Item name, Quantity
- Tables scale horizontally
- Each row contains its own entity
- The purpose of partitioning is to group things together

It should look something like:
PartitionKey	RowKey			UserName	ListName		ItemName	Quantity
user123			list1_item1		Alice		Weekly shop		Milk		2
user123			list1_item2		Alice		Weekly shop 	Bread 		1
user123			list2_item1		Alice 		Party snacks	Chips		3
user312			list1_item1		Bob			Lunch			Sandwich	2

If user also consists of their phone number, a new column would be added:
	Phone
	123-123
	123-123
	123-123
	111-111
! No new row !

CAP Theorum:
- Can deliver only 2 of the 3 desired characteristics
- Consistency
  - All clients see the same data at the same time
- Availability
  - Any client that makes a request gets a response
- Partition Tolerance
  - a communication break within a distributed system

CP database - when a partition occurs between any two nodes, the system has to shut down the non-consisten node until the partition is resolved.
AP database - when a partition occurs, all notes remain available but those at the wrong end of a partition might return an older version of the data.
CA database - it can’t do this if there is a partition between any two nodes in the system, however, and therefore can’t deliver fault tolerance.

Azure Cosmos DB, Paritioning:
https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/cosmos-db/partitioning

CAP Theorum:
https://www.ibm.com/think/topics/cap-theorem

-------------------------------------------------------

Transaction (process) - Unit of work (Terminology)
- When processing multiple things at the same time
- This makes sure they both fail or succeed together

DbContext is a unit of work because it is 'Scoped' (Scoped = per request.
	Everything that happens between the request and response = 1 unit of work).
	It trackc changes until it becomes a response

SaveChanges() triggers the commit the changes to DB

Distributed systems, each domain are on their own, but you want Eventual Consistency

